                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "At x = 0 the gradient remains positive on both sides, so there is no turning point. Part c confirms a change of concavity, making (0, 3) a horizontal point of inflection. At x = 3 the gradient changes from positive to negative, so (3, 30) is a local maximum.",
